cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Statement Codec: reference implementation for verifiable attributed quotations"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Onishi
    given-names: Tatsuki
version: "0.4"
date-released: "2026-10-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/bougtoir/statement-codec"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of a verification contract for attributed
  statements: signed statements, signed span quotations with positional
  context constraints, bitemporal validity/commitment semantics, consent
  manifests, and a hash-chained audit log. All benchmark data are synthetic.
keywords:
  - provenance
  - quotation integrity
  - bitemporal data
  - audit logs
  - verifiable credentials
